          %p We now unwind again how this comes about and what it all means:
          %p
            First, the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            holds at 0 means that there is a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"}> proof
            \-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mn 0
                    %mi P
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\vdash \;\; 0_P \,\colon\, P(0)
                  \\,.
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            for 0 that gives
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(0)
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of the given display map
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DisplayMapInterpretingNDependentType"} (6)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mn 0
                            %mo *
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  0^* P &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; P
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                  \\\
                  * &amp;\underset{0}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbb{N}
                  }
          %p
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 0
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0_P
            is interpreted as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of the resulting fibration over the terminal object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mn 0
                            %mo *
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  *
                  \&amp;\overset{p_0}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  0^* P
                  \&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;
                  P
                  \\\
                  \&amp;\searrow&amp; \big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  *
                  \&amp;\underset{0}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbb{N}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            But by the defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  * &amp;\stackrel{p_0}{\longrightarrow}&amp; P
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                  \\\
                  * &amp;\underset{0}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbb{N}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Next the induction step. Formally it says that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/implication"} implication
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi succ
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} succ_P(n) \,\colon\, P(n) \to P(n+1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi succ
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  n \in \mathbb{N}
                  \\;\;\;\vdash\;\;\;
                  succ_P(n) \,\colon\, P(n) \to   P(n+1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mo *
                          %mo ⊔
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mo ≔
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi s
                            %mo *
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℕ
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P\big(\ast \sqcup (-)\big) \coloneqq
                  \&amp; s^*P &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; P
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \mathbb{N} &amp;\underset{s}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbb{N}
                  }
          %p
            and the interpretation of the implication term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi succ
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} succ_P(n)
            is as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mo *
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to s^* P
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/\mathbb{N}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi s
                            %mo *
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℕ
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P
                  \&amp; \overset{p_s}{\longrightarrow} &amp;
                  s^*P &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; P
                  \\\
                  \&amp;\searrow &amp; \big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{N} &amp;\overset{s}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbb{N}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Again by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the pullback this is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi succ
                                %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℕ
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P &amp;\overset{succ_P}{\longrightarrow}&amp; P
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{N}
                  \&amp;\underset{s}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\mathbb{N}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p In summary this shows that
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              being a proposition depending on natural numbers which holds at 0 and which holds at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
              if it holds at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            is interpreted precisely as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+for+an+endofunctor"} endofunctor-algebra homomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{N}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheEndofunctor"} (1)
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction+principle"} induction principle
            is supposed to deduce from this that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            holds for every
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ind
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ind(n) \colon P(n)
            for all
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ind
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  n \,\colon\, \mathbb{N}
                  \\;\;\;\vdash\;\;\;
                  ind(n) \,\colon\, P(n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The categorical interpretation of this is as a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \,\colon\, \mathbb{N} \to P
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/\mathbb{N}}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InferenceRules"}
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            gives.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"}> natural numbers
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
            %li
