            as an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+type"} inductive type
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Martin-Löf84"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"} Per Martin-Löf
                (notes by
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Sambin"} Giovanni Sambin
                %a{:href => "/nlab/files/MartinLofIntuitionisticTypeTheory.pdf#page=44"} pp. 38
                of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Intuitionistic type theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://archive-pml.github.io/martin-lof/pdfs/Bibliopolis-Book-retypeset-1984.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MartinLofIntuitionisticTypeTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#CoquandPaulin90
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"}> Thierry Coquand
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christine+Paulin"} Christine Paulin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Inductively defined types
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 417
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-52335-9_47"} doi:10.1007/3-540-52335-9_47
            %li#Paulin-Mohring93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christine+Paulin-Mohring"}> Christine Paulin-Mohring
                , §1.3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Inductive definitions in the system Coq – Rules and Properties
                %em Typed Lambda Calculi and Applications
                TLCA 1993, Lecture Notes in Computer Science
                %strong 664
                Springer (1993) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0037116"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0037116
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Dybjer94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Dybjer"}> Peter Dybjer
                , §3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Inductive families
                %strong 6
                (1994) 440–465
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01211308"} doi:10.1007/BF01211308
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01211308"} doi:10.1007/BF01211308
                %a{:href => "http://www.cse.chalmers.se/~peterd/papers/Inductive_Families.pdf"} pdf
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            The syntax in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
          %ul
            %li#Paulin-Mohring14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christine+Paulin-Mohring"}> Christine Paulin-Mohring
              , p. 6 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Introduction to the Calculus of Inductive Constructions
              %em Vienna Summer of Logic
              (2014) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://hal.inria.fr/hal-01094195"}> hal:01094195
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://hal.inria.fr/hal-01094195/document"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://easychair.org/smart-program/VSL2014/APPA-invited-slides-6.pdf"} pdf slides
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Pfenning
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Pfenning"}> Frank Pfenning
              ,
              %em Lecture notes on natural numbers
              (2009) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.cs.cmu.edu/~fp/courses/15317-f09/lectures/06-nat.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Pfenning-NaturalNumbersType.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in a context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            and in view of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+types"} higher inductive types
          %ul
            %li#UFP13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
                , §1.9 in:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
                (2013) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/book/"}> web
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://hottheory.files.wordpress.com/2013/03/hott-online-323-g28e4374.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"}> Egbert Rijke
                , §3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Type+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.11082"} arXiv:2212.11082
            %li{:id => "Söhnen18"}
              %p
                Kajetan Söhnen, §2.4.5 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher Inductive Types in Homotopy Type Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.lmu.de/~petrakis/Soehnen.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Soehnen-HigherInductiveTypes.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#LumsdaineShulman17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"}> Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Semantics of higher inductive types
                %strong 169
                (2020) 159-208 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.07088"}> arXiv:1705.07088
                , talk slides
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/papers/cellcxs.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S030500411900015X"} doi:10.1017/S030500411900015X
          %p Equivalence to binary presentations:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  Nicolas Magaud
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Nicolas+Magaud"} ?
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Yves Bertot
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Yves+Bertot"} ?
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Changing Data Structures in Type Theory: A Study of Natural Numbers
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Types for Proofs and Programs. TYPES 2000
                %strong 2277
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-45842-5_12"}> doi:10.1007/3-540-45842-5_12
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dpt-info.u-strasbg.fr/~magaud/papers/types2000-nmagaud.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  Nicolas Magaud
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Nicolas+Magaud"} ?
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Changing Data Representation within the Coq
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Theorem Proving in Higher Order Logics. TPHOLs 2003
                %strong 2758
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/10930755_6"}> doi:10.1007/10930755_6
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Some discussion about the large recursion principle of the natural numbers type in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory+with+type+variables"} dependent type theory with type variables
            occurs in:
          %ul
            %li#CTZulip
              %em> Dependent Type Theory vs Polymorphic Type Theory
              , Category Theory Zulip (
              %a{:href => "https://categorytheory.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/229199-learning.3A-questions/topic/Dependent.20Type.20Theory.20vs.20Polymorphic.20Type.20Theory"}> web
              )
          %p
            That one can construct the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
            from the integers type can be found in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Sattler"}> Christian Sattler
              ,
              %em Natural numbers from integers
              (
              %a{:href => "https://www.cse.chalmers.se/~sattler/docs/naturals.pdf"}> pdf
